 ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-19T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Boulder, CO; Douglas, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Weld, CO; Denver, CO; Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bcd88b1b66192e2d43a08e5556c874386ead632c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-18T23:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 182347 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 547 PM MDT Tue Aug 18 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered showers and thunderstorms this afternoon into tonight. A couple strong to severe storms possible across the eastern plains later this evening. - Isolated storms again for Wednesday, though chances of stronger storms shift to the south. - Warming ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-18T18:40:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Wednesday...Isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms are expected this afternoon, mainly across the northeastern plains. Variable and gusty outflow winds will be possible with any convection that develops, with a few of the stronger storms producing some briefly heavy rainfall. Temperatures this afternoon will be near or a little above normal, with humidi","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"cht01","station_name":"Chatfield at South Platte Reserv